  "tactics": {
    "styleTags": [
      "High press",
      "Fast transitions",
      "Wide rotations"
    ],
    "tacticalNote": "France doesn't possess and probe — they press, recover, and explode. Mbappé and Dembélé swap flanks to confuse fullbacks while a #10 drops centrally. The transition is the system. In 10 seconds from a turnover, they can be in your net.",
    "strength": "Counter-attack speed is unmatched — overcommit forward and France punishes you in three passes.",
    "vulnerability": "Slow to set their shape after losing the ball — direct teams with pace in behind can exploit the high line."
  },
  "watchFor": [
    "Mbappé's movement off the ball — he drifts left and pulls center-backs, opening lanes for runners from deep.",
    "Tchouaméni's cover shadow before the press triggers — his body angle tells you where the ball is going.",
    "Deschamps' substitutions around the 65th minute — they telegraph exactly how France intends to close the game."
  ],
